Algorithm 

Step 1: Start the program.

Step 2: Input the number of sensors and communication links.

Step 3: Represent each sensor as a vertex and each communication link as a weighted, undirected edge.

Step 4: Initialize all sensors as unvisited and set the total cost to zero.

Step 5: Select a starting sensor and mark it as visited.

Step 6: Find the minimum-weight edge connecting a visited sensor to an unvisited sensor.

Step 7: If such an edge exists, select it, display the communication link and its weight, add the weight to the total cost, and mark the new sensor as visited.

Step 8: Repeat Steps 6 and 7 until no eligible edge remains.

Step 9: Display the selected links and the total communication cost of the resulting spanning tree or forest.

Step 10: Identify and display any sensors that remain unconnected to the starting sensor.

Step 11: Stop the program.
